\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {III}{\ignorespaces  Top~5 eROSITA anomalies with SIMBAD novelty status (``Novel'' $=$ no SIMBAD counterpart within a $5''$ cone search; \S  \ref {sec:simbad}). All are located near the LMC or Galactic plane. \textbf  {Warning on $S_{\rm  BigAE}$ column:} the production score-axis ($0.259$ threshold) could not be reconciled with the committed raw-score artifact on any of 16 monotone rescalings $+$ 3 IsolationForest retrains, and the top-5 $S_{\rm  BigAE}$ values are non-monotone in the committed raw artifact (Spearman $\rho = -0.10$). \textbf  {Do not use $S_{\rm  BigAE}$ as a continuous science data product or for score-weighted analysis; the committed, reproducible selection is the $n=298$ membership list (ranked by the committed raw score artifact).} See \S  \ref {sec:erosita} and \href  {https://github.com/Hubify-Projects/bigbounce/blob/main/pipelines/p3\_anomaly\_engine/r24conf\_erosita\_axis\_sweep.json}{\nolinkurl  {pipelines/p3\_anomaly\_engine/r24conf\_erosita\_axis\_sweep.json}}. Column $S_{\rm  IF,raw}$ is the IsolationForest raw isolation-score value (anomaly\_score on a $\sim 0$--$3.5\times 10^{4}$ scale, reported by the 100-tree IF detector trained on the 16-d \textsc  {BigAE}{} latent feature space and used as the cross-validation diagnostic of \S  \ref {sec:pathc_caveats}~(ii)); IF raw scores are \emph  {not} a parallel catalog axis but are tabulated here so readers can map between the two detectors.}}{10}{table.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:erosita_top}{{III}{10}{Top~5 eROSITA anomalies with SIMBAD novelty status (``Novel'' $=$ no SIMBAD counterpart within a $5''$ cone search; \S \ref {sec:simbad}). All are located near the LMC or Galactic plane. \textbf {Warning on $S_{\rm BigAE}$ column:} the production score-axis ($0.259$ threshold) could not be reconciled with the committed raw-score artifact on any of 16 monotone rescalings $+$ 3 IsolationForest retrains, and the top-5 $S_{\rm BigAE}$ values are non-monotone in the committed raw artifact (Spearman $\rho = -0.10$). \textbf {Do not use $S_{\rm BigAE}$ as a continuous science data product or for score-weighted analysis; the committed, reproducible selection is the $n=298$ membership list (ranked by the committed raw score artifact).} See \S \ref {sec:erosita} and \artifact {pipelines/p3\_anomaly\_engine/r24conf\_erosita\_axis\_sweep.json}. Column $S_{\rm IF,raw}$ is the IsolationForest raw isolation-score value (anomaly\_score on a $\sim 0$--$3.5\times 10^{4}$ scale, reported by the 100-tree IF detector trained on the 16-d \BigAE {} latent feature space and used as the cross-validation diagnostic of \S \ref {sec:pathc_caveats}~(ii)); IF raw scores are \emph {not} a parallel catalog axis but are tabulated here so readers can map between the two detectors}{table.3}{}}
