\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces  Multi-tracer Fisher $\sigma (f_{\rm  NL})$ vs.\ tracer number density $\bar  n$ for the canonical 5-tracer configuration of \S  \ref {sec:fnl}. The dashed gray line marks the dense-tracer limit ($\sigma (f_{\rm  NL})= 11.71$); the dotted dark-red line marks the single-tracer baseline ($\sigma (f_{\rm  NL})= 16.85$). Vertical orange and goldenrod lines mark the gold ($\bar  n = 8.5\times 10^{-6}$) and silver ($\bar  n = 4.5\times 10^{-5}$) anomaly sub-samples. The Heinrich-\textit  {et~al.}\ \S  IV $15$--$30\%$ Fisher-info penalty range corresponds to $\sigma (f_{\rm  NL})= 12.56$--$13.35$ at the canonical configuration. \emph  {Normalization note:} the $\sigma (f_{\rm  NL})= 16.85$ single-tracer baseline and $\sigma (f_{\rm  NL})= 11.71$ dense-tracer limit quoted here are internal to the shot-noise Fisher implementation underlying this figure (a 5-tracer DESI QSO/LRG/BGS $+$ gold/silver-anomaly configuration evaluated with a simplified analytic power-law $P(k)$ over a single effective volume); they are \emph  {not} on the same absolute normalization as the redshift-binned Fisher of \S  \ref {sec:fnl}, whose canonical single-tracer DESI-QSO baseline is $\sigma (f_{\rm  NL})^{\rm  std} = 8.98$. Only the relative quantities of this figure --- the $+7.93\%$ dense-limit improvement and the $15$--$30\%$ shot-noise penalty mapping --- carry over to the \S  \ref {sec:fnl} forecast; absolute $\sigma (f_{\rm  NL})$ values should be read from \S  \ref {sec:fnl}.}}{21}{figure.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:shotnoise_sensitivity}{{11}{21}{Multi-tracer Fisher $\sigfnl $ vs.\ tracer number density $\bar n$ for the canonical 5-tracer configuration of \S \ref {sec:fnl}. The dashed gray line marks the dense-tracer limit ($\sigfnl = 11.71$); the dotted dark-red line marks the single-tracer baseline ($\sigfnl = 16.85$). Vertical orange and goldenrod lines mark the gold ($\bar n = 8.5\times 10^{-6}$) and silver ($\bar n = 4.5\times 10^{-5}$) anomaly sub-samples. The Heinrich-\etal \^^M\S IV $15$--$30\%$ Fisher-info penalty range corresponds to $\sigfnl = 12.56$--$13.35$ at the canonical configuration. \emph {Normalization note:} the $\sigfnl = 16.85$ single-tracer baseline and $\sigfnl = 11.71$ dense-tracer limit quoted here are internal to the shot-noise Fisher implementation underlying this figure (a 5-tracer DESI QSO/LRG/BGS $+$ gold/silver-anomaly configuration evaluated with a simplified analytic power-law $P(k)$ over a single effective volume); they are \emph {not} on the same absolute normalization as the redshift-binned Fisher of \S \ref {sec:fnl}, whose canonical single-tracer DESI-QSO baseline is $\sigfnl ^{\rm std} = 8.98$. Only the relative quantities of this figure --- the $+7.93\%$ dense-limit improvement and the $15$--$30\%$ shot-noise penalty mapping --- carry over to the \S \ref {sec:fnl} forecast; absolute $\sigfnl $ values should be read from \S \ref {sec:fnl}}{figure.11}{}}
